[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Hovercraft]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:01.06]Lesson 29 | 第29课
[00:02.96]The hovercraft | 气垫船
[00:10.31]What is a hovercraft riding on when it is in motion? | 气垫船行驶时靠的是什么？
[00:16.55]Many strange new means of transport have been developed in our century, | 本世纪研制出了许多新奇的交通工具，
[00:22.29]the strangest of them being perhaps the hovercraft. | 其中最新奇的也许要数气垫船了。
[00:27.29]In 1953, a former electronics engineer in his fifties, Christopher Cockerell, | 1953年，一位50多岁、名叫克里斯托弗·科克雷尔的原电子工程师，
[00:35.44]who had turned to boat-building on the Norfolk Broads, | 他当时已在诺福克郡布罗兹区改行制造小船，
[00:39.52]suggested an idea on which he had been working for many years to the British Government and industrial circles. | 把他研究了多年的一种想法提交给了英国政府和工业界。
[00:48.13]It was the idea of supporting a craft on a 'pad', or cushion, of low-pressure air, ringed with a curtain of higher pressure air. | 这个想法是：让船支承在一个低压空气“垫”或气垫上，四周以一圈较高压力的空气环绕。
[01:00.20]Ever since, people have had difficulty in deciding whether the craft should be ranged among ships, planes, | 从那时起，人们一直难以确定这种船该归入船舶、飞机
[01:09.38]or land vehicles--for it is something in between a boat and an aircraft. | 还是陆地交通工具——因为它介于小船与飞机之间。
[01:17.57]As a shipbuilder, Cockerell was trying to find a solution to the problem of the wave resistance which wastes a good deal of a surface ship's power and limits its speed. | 作为一位造船者，科克雷尔当时正试图解决波浪阻力问题，这种阻力浪费了水面船只的大量动力，限制了它的速度。
[01:31.54]His answer was to lift the vessel out of the water by making it ride on a cushion of air, no more than one or two feet thick. | 他的答案是：让船骑在一个厚度不超过一、二英尺的气垫上，从而把船体抬出水面。
[01:42.60]This is done by a great number of ring-shaped air jets on the bottom of the craft. | 这是靠船底部的大量环形空气喷嘴完成的。
[01:49.60]It 'flies', therefore, but it cannot fly higher--its action depends on the surface, water or ground, over which it rides. | 因此它能“飞”，但飞不高——它的动作取决于它所行驶的水面或地面。
[02:02.29]The first tests on the Solent in 1959 caused a sensation. | 1959年在索伦特海峡进行的第一次试航引起了轰动。
[02:08.57]The hovercraft travelled first over the water, then mounted the beach, climbed up the dunes, and sat down on a road. | 气垫船先是在水面上行驶，然后登上海滩，爬上沙丘，最后停在了公路上。
[02:19.57]Later it crossed the Channel, riding smoothly over the waves, which presented no problem. | 后来它驶过了海峡，平稳地行驶在波浪之上，波浪根本不在话下。
[02:28.89]Since that time, various types of hovercraft have appeared and taken up regular service. | 从那以后，各式各样的气垫船出现了，并投入了定期营运。
[02:36.31]The hovercraft is particularly useful in large areas with poor communications such as Africa or Australia; | 在非洲或澳大利亚这类交通不便的广大地区，气垫船特别有用；
[02:44.82]it can become a 'flying fruit-bowl', carrying bananas from the plantations to the ports; | 它可以成为一只“飞行水果篮”，把香蕉从种植园运到港口；
[02:51.89]giant hovercraft liners could span the Atlantic; | 巨型气垫班船或许能够横渡大西洋；
[02:55.67]and the railway of the future may well be the 'hovertrain', | 未来的铁路也许就是“气垫火车”，
[02:59.99]riding on its air cushion over a single rail, which it never touches, at speeds, up to 300 m.p.h.--the possibilities appear unlimited. | 它骑在单轨上方的气垫上，永不接触铁轨，时速可达300英里——前景似乎无限广阔。
